Task 2: Finding files containing specific strings.

Navigate to the users directory.
>> analyst@f8ed80368369:~/logs$ cd /home/analyst/reports/users
>> analyst@f8ed80368369:~/reports/users$ 

Using the pipe character to output the ls command to the grep command to list only the files conatining the string Q1 in their names.
>> analyst@f8ed80368369:~/reports/users$ ls|grep Q1
Output: Q1_access.txt Q1_added_users.txt Q1_deleted_users.txt

List the files that contain the word access in the names using grep. 
>> analyst@f8ed80368369:~/reports/users$ ls|grep access
Output: Q1_access.txt Q2_access.txt Q3_access.txt Q4_access.txt

